      "side": 1,
      "message": "That runs the formatter on *every* file in the repo.\n\njj formatters have a very specific API. They must output to stdout rather than writing to files, and they must read from stdin.\n\nThis allows you to run `jj fix` on a revision, and the whole chain of commits gets formatted correctly. If you were to just run tools/run_formatter.sh, you would only be able to format the current commit, and if you were to run it on the current commit you would introduce merge conflicts in the child.",
